---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { AUTH_CONTACT, TERMS_LAST_UPDATED } from '../../data/auth';
import PolicyNav from '../../components/PolicyNav.astro';
---

<Layout title="auth.mss.io Terms of Use — legal.mss.io" width="max-w-[760px]" headerPadding="pb-10 sm:pb-12">
<PolicyNav slot="subnav" current="terms" />
<!-- Main Editorial Content Area -->
<main class="flex-1 pt-8 sm:pt-10 space-y-12 sm:space-y-14">
<!-- Document Title & Meta Header -->
<section class="space-y-3 pb-8 border-b border-neutral-200/80 dark:border-neutral-800/80">
<div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500">
          auth.mss.io
        </div>
<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50">
          Terms of Use
        </h1>
<p class="text-base sm:text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
          The rules for using your MSS account. Last updated {TERMS_LAST_UPDATED}.
        </p>
</section>
<!-- Section 1 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          1. About the service
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            auth.mss.io (the "Service") is a sign-in and identity service operated by Mario Stefano Suharja, doing business as MSS, based in Calgary, Alberta, Canada ("MSS", "we", "us"). It lets you create an account once and use it to sign in to websites and applications that MSS runs or that rely on MSS for sign-in ("Connected Applications").
          </p>
<p>
            By creating an account or signing in through the Service, you agree to these Terms of Use and to our <a class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors" href="/auth/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
          </p>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Section 2 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          2. Eligibility and your account
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            You must be at least 13 years old to use the Service. If you are under the age of majority where you live (18 in Alberta), you may use it only with the involvement of a parent or guardian who agrees to these Terms.
          </p>
<p class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
            You agree to:
          </p>
<ul class="list-disc list-outside pl-5 space-y-2">
<li>Give accurate information when you register, and keep it current.</li>
<li>Keep your password, recovery codes and multi-factor authentication devices secure, and not share your account.</li>
<li>Tell us promptly at <a class="font-mono text-sm underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors" href={`mailto:${AUTH_CONTACT}`}>{AUTH_CONTACT}</a> if you believe your account has been accessed without permission.</li>
</ul>
<p>
            You are responsible for activity under your account unless it results from our failure to take reasonable security measures. If you sign in with a third-party account (for example Google, GitHub or Apple), that provider's terms also apply to that account.
          </p>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Section 3 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          3. Acceptable use
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            Use the Service only to sign in to Connected Applications you are allowed to use. You must not:
          </p>
<ul class="list-disc list-outside pl-5 space-y-2">
<li>Access or try to access accounts, data or systems you are not authorized to use.</li>
<li>Probe, scan or test the Service for vulnerabilities, or bypass rate limits, MFA or other security controls, except as described below.</li>
<li>Use automated means (bots, credential stuffing, scripted sign-ups) to create accounts or sign in.</li>
<li>Interfere with or overload the Service, or attempt to reverse engineer it beyond what the law allows.</li>
<li>Impersonate another person or use the Service for anything unlawful.</li>
</ul>
<div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200/80 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-white dark:bg-[#13161f] text-sm space-y-1">
<div class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Security reports</div>
<p class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-normal">
              If you find a security issue, please report it privately to <a class="font-mono underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors" href={`mailto:${AUTH_CONTACT}`}>{AUTH_CONTACT}</a> and give us reasonable time to fix it before disclosure. We will not pursue action against good-faith research that avoids privacy violations, data destruction and service disruption.
            </p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Section 4 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          4. Connected Applications
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            The Service only handles sign-in. Each Connected Application is responsible for its own content and features, and may have its own terms and privacy policy. When you sign in to a Connected Application, you will see which account details it is requesting (for example your email address or name) before they are shared.
          </p>
<p>
            Where a Connected Application is run by MSS for a client, that client's own terms may also apply to your use of that application.
          </p>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Section 5 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          5. Availability, changes and termination
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            The Service is provided on a best-effort basis. It may be unavailable at times for maintenance, upgrades or reasons outside our control, and we do not guarantee any particular uptime. We do not currently keep backups of account data, so if data is lost we may be unable to restore your account and you may need to register again.
          </p>
<p>
            We may change, suspend or discontinue the Service or any feature. Where practical, we will give reasonable notice before discontinuing it entirely.
          </p>
<p>
            We may suspend or close your account if you breach these Terms, if your account poses a security risk, or if required by law. You can stop using the Service at any time and ask us to delete your account at <a class="font-mono text-sm underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors" href={`mailto:${AUTH_CONTACT}`}>{AUTH_CONTACT}</a>. Sections 6 and 7 survive termination.
          </p>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Section 6 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          6. Disclaimers and limitation of liability
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            To the extent permitted by law, the Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.
          </p>
<p>
            To the extent permitted by law, MSS is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, data or goodwill, arising from your use of the Service. Our total liability for any claim relating to the Service is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us for the Service in the 12 months before the claim, or CAD $100.
          </p>
<p>
            You agree to indemnify MSS against claims and costs arising from your breach of these Terms or misuse of the Service.
          </p>
<p>
            Nothing in these Terms limits rights you have under consumer protection laws that cannot be waived by contract.
          </p>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Section 7 -->
<section class="space-y-4">
<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
          7. Governing law, changes and contact
        </h2>
<div class="space-y-3 text-[15px] sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
<p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Alberta and the federal laws of Canada that apply there. You and MSS agree to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Alberta, sitting in Calgary, unless the law where you live gives you a right to bring a claim elsewhere.
          </p>
<p>
            We may update these Terms. We will change the "Last updated" date above, and for material changes we will notify you by email or at sign-in before they take effect. Continuing to use the Service after that means you accept the updated Terms.
          </p>
<p>
            If any part of these Terms is found unenforceable, the rest stays in effect. These Terms and the Privacy Policy are the whole agreement between you and MSS about the Service.
          </p>
<p>
            Questions: <a class="font-mono text-sm underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors" href={`mailto:${AUTH_CONTACT}`}>{AUTH_CONTACT}</a>, Mario Stefano Suharja, Calgary, Alberta, Canada.
          </p>
</div>
</section>
<!-- Contact Section matching legal.mss.io -->
<section aria-labelledby="contact-heading" class="pt-6 border-t border-neutral-200/80 dark:border-neutral-800/80">
<h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold text-neutral-400 dark:text-neutral-500 font-mono mb-4" id="contact-heading">
          Contact
        </h2>
<dl class="space-y-3.5 text-sm">
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between py-1 gap-1">
<dt class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Questions about these Terms</dt>
<dd>
<a class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-200 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-4 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm transition-colors" href={`mailto:${AUTH_CONTACT}`}>
                {AUTH_CONTACT}
              </a>
</dd>
</div>
<div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between py-1 gap-1">
<dt class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Report a security issue</dt>
<dd>
<a class="text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-200 hover:text-accent dark:hover:text-accent-dark underline decoration-neutral-300 dark:decoration-neutral-700 underline-offset-4 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm transition-colors" href={`mailto:${AUTH_CONTACT}`}>
                {AUTH_CONTACT}
              </a>
</dd>
</div>
</dl>
</section>
</main>
<a slot="footer-links" class="hover:text-neutral-800 dark:hover:text-neutral-300 hover:underline transition-colors" href="/auth/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
</Layout>
